Many thanks to jjn@sanger.ac.uk who gave us the following info

The Fore documentation about anycast addresses relate to UNI version
4. This isn't supported on DU. When 'making up' anycast addresses just
change the first byte for 0x47, like a 'normal' nsap address...

>
> Thanks for the reply.  I am still not really getting anywhere with this.
>

> Can you tell me when these anycast addresses are created.  Do you give
> each card a manual address or let the ATM switch issue one to the card
> on startup ?  Our networks people that the FORE switches we use only
> use UNI3.0 and 3.1 but they seem unsure.  How would I go about
> changing an anycast address.

The anycast address is set up on the DLE services. It would have been
assigned when the LANE services were set up.

There is no special configuration required on the NIC card.

When the LANE services are set up on the switch (conf lane les) you'd
specify the anycast address.

So basically we need to make a config change to the anycast address on the FORE
switches.  Obviously this is not something we can just do without some detailed
testing (i.e will our other servers with FORE cards still work with a updated
anycast address ?).  I'll post more info in the new year.






