From: Joel Votaw <jovotaw () cs ! nmsu ! edu>
Date: Mon, 20 Dec 1999 17:35:35 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: SCSI cards for AlphaPC 164
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079091516460


I mailed out about a week ago asking what SCSI adaptors work on an
AlphaPC 164.  The support base is limited because of what SRM will
recognize and boot off of; and you have to buy *some* kind of SCSI card
since Tru64 doesn't support the IDE adaptor on those motherboards.

The short answer:

Buy an NCR/Symbios 53c875 -based card; the generic/reference/OEM one works
fine. The Tru64 kernel will complain when it starts up ("unsupported
53c875-based adaptor" or something like that) but will work anyways. 
These cards can be had for $70 including 2-day shipping from
www.centrix-intl.com and I'm sure there are other places online as well. 


