To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] : 3.2g to 4.0d upgrade.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079091516342

Hello all,

The up grade went ahead without any major problems (yet).  As the system is
not being used much now its hard to say if the upgrade was a complete
success.  Mainly disks exported using nfs. i.e there is no major load.

Thanks for all replies I will attach all to this message. The message from
Bruce B Platt has a script which tars up all files necessary to write to new
installation. which would be very usseful if you had to do a few machines as
i only had the one to do i just printed it out and used it as a checklist
for the files i copied to the nfs drive.

What i did was.

Shutdown oracle Databases.
vdump of every disk on the sytem to tapes.
used cp -pR to copy /etc,/usr to nfsdisk on another machine.
made sure I had most important files
/var/adm/lmf/*
/etc/fstab
/etc/fdmns
/etc/exports
/etc/passwd etc,
installed 4.0d on new disk rz5c.
ran netsetup,bindsetup,nissetup.
once these were running successfully
mounted nfs disk where i copied all etc and usr to.
copied back license files fdmns etc.
mount all disk back one at a time manually and when no problem added them to
/etc/fstab.
startup of oracle databases when showed no problems coopied necessary bootup
files into /sbin/init.d/rc[0,3].d

As regards the files I copied to the nfs i didnt really need them as i just
remounted the old root and user disks and copied all info from there.

Thanks again,
Darrell

