From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Dec 10 20:12:40 1999
From: "Daniel L. Schwartz" <expresso () snip ! net>
Date: Fri, 10 Dec 1999 20:12:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: 164SX conversion woes - Summary so far
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079091516283



	First off, I want to thank Russ Fish, Dr. Tom Leitner, and Robert
Maiello for the help so far.


	But before I start, Compaq needs to get their act together in two major
areas:


	1) We need a Hardware Compatibility List (HCL), similar to the one
Microsoft has at:

 <<www.microsoft.com/hwtest/hcl>. This is important as more and more
people  migrate their machines from AlphaNT to Tru64 (and OpenVMS); and
especially so since Compaq is trading in NT licenses for Tru64 and
OpenVMS to help soothe the pain;


	2) The Tru64 documentation *sucks* - There is no installation
troubleshooting guide included on the six Tru64 CD's.



	Here are the suggestions so far, and my comments:


	Robert Maiello wrote:


>>>>

<excerpt>

I'm not familar with this hardware or Tru64 on ide.  


Perhaps Tru64 does not support your CDROM drive? 


Also, some of our Alphas (much older than yours) needed a jumper 
changed

on

the CDROM drive depending whether one was running NT or VMS/UNIX.   


The next message on the screen should be something like "xxxxx is a

valid

boot block .."


Good luck.


Robert Maiello

Toys R Us Unix Group

maiellor@toysrus.com



</excerpt><<<<<<<<


	Hmmm, the drive worked flawlessly when the machine was running AlphaNT,
including being recognized in AlphaBIOS 5.62 during the initial NT4
installation from the distribution CD...


	Dr. Tom Leitner wrote:


>>>>

<excerpt>

On Fri, 10 Dec 1999, Daniel L. Schwartz wrote:


> dqa0.0.0.108.0	DQAO		ATAPI 40X CD CDROM DRIVE VER 2.B1


[...]


> jumping to bootstrap code

> 

> 	And here is where it hangs...


I suspect that the CD-ROM drive is flakey or not properly supported.

Unix uses a block-size of 512bytes while most PC CD-ROM drives

use 2048 bytes. Some SCSI drives can be switched by software to 512 
byte

blocks, others, like many Plextor drives have a jumper for that.


Try to get a Toshiba or Plextor SCSI CD-ROM for booting for 
installation

CD.


Tom



</excerpt><<<<<<<<


	Notice that in the note below that the CD/ROM was indeed being
controlled by SRM, because I could hear the CD drive spinning back up and
the front panel light flashing...


	And Russ Fish wrote...


>>>>

<excerpt>

Hi Dan--

Sorry, I missed what you were trying to do (boot from the CD-ROM). You're
right,

the kernel should be fine. I wonder whether that ATAPI drive is
recognized by

*any* T64U kernel, though--I bet not. You can check this in the
supported

options catalog on http://www.digital.com/alphaserver

--Russ


